    "body": "The event delivery chain conflicted with current main, and its older adapter overwrote stronger deletion, dependency-approval and RACI guards. This consolidation preserves the source histories through #417 plus the additional #339 successor, while retaining current integrity, authenticated-session revocation, source identity and migration ancestry.\n\nMain `f8925e339447cb593f7cce5d86403d1396aaf5a5`, including approved editorial ownership PR475, is normally merged into this branch at `08acdfa897832c42ef1582f26ffdd7c23f019b4c`. The web publication-selection behavior and event follow flow coexist; generated API clients reproduce exactly. Mobile companion [TDF-mobile#115](https://github.com/diegueins680/TDF-mobile/pull/115) is pinned at `ede1f2a0ccf75f3794c7892f291e1751b279d19e`, which preserves both previous mobile histories. It was independently approved and concurrently merged at `bca7f39cebcae24b62a4404bf5fd76bb9328f95a`; both mobile post-merge workflows passed, and this pinned source SHA is retained in mobile main ancestry.\n\nLatest lifecycle repair at `34ca75d3d92d2a6def22e63ddd47baa96edca878`: the enabled feature-flag row is share-locked through each lifecycle transaction. Receipt validation now runs inside the same session transaction and binds event, UUID, target state and next version before commit; its private exception retains the existing `invalid_database_response` HTTP500 contract. Eight injected corrupt SQL returns prove rollback of state, transition, audit and receipt rows.\n\nCurrent repair validation: the Stack-compiled authenticated HTTP/database-boundary harness passes 110 examples. Actual PostgreSQL16 reproduces the old flag race and passes the fixed implementation for both race orders at READ COMMITTED, REPEATABLE READ and SERIALIZABLE, plus all existing migration/replay/rollback assertions. Five unchanged catalog regression tests, the strict 1,171-candidate gate, three inventory tests, shell syntax and the repository formal gate pass. All 160 registered production migrations are unchanged; the corrected lifecycle adapter remains unregistered and disabled by default. Current-head hosted application tests, bounded TLC/Alloy checks and fresh independent approval remain required.\n\nThe earlier follow repair makes successful follow/unfollow writes refresh shared viewer and artist caches even after navigation. Navigation and analytics effects remain bound to their original profile/session lifetime. The logistics task CTA is deferred while adapter migrations are outside the production manifest and `event.operations.api` is disabled. The direct task route and isolated enabled-adapter validation remain intact. Two historical catalog successor mappings now point to the current reviewed sources; original decision payloads, previous successor IDs, source provenance and all regression assertions are preserved.\n\nReconciliation validation at `08acdfa` (before the lifecycle review fix): five unchanged catalog regression tests, the strict 1,171-candidate catalog gate, 83 release tests, 32 CI configuration tests, repository quality, formal verification and regenerated specification inventory pass. The only textual merge conflict was the catalog decision list; all event decisions are retained, and both new main decisions are exact. The two migration successor mappings now reference the 160-entry registry, retaining their complete prior mappings. The production manifest exactly matches main and the mobile pin is unchanged. Hosted checks on `08acdfa` passed; subsequent review found the lifecycle defects fixed below. Those results do not substitute for current-head CI.\n\nPreviously executed implementation validation (historical heads; current-head hosted checks remain mandatory):\n- Current merged application: complete Stack build; freshly built Hspec executable passed 3,576 examples with zero failures and six existing separate-runner cases pending in that executable. The unchanged production-auth HTTP harness passed 107 cases against an isolated native PostgreSQL16 database, which was removed afterward.\n- Current merged UI: 241 suites / 2,648 tests, production build and initial bundle budget passed. After the latest follow/link repair: 27 focused UI tests, including delayed follow/unfollow completion and all existing logout/session/navigation guards, passed; zero-warning lint and typecheck passed.\n- Five unchanged catalog regression tests, the full 1,170-candidate no-unreviewed/no-stale gate, regenerated specification inventory, 83 release tests, 32 CI contract tests, repository quality and the unchanged dependency-security gate passed. Security-policy success does not mean zero dependency findings.\n- Hosted validation on the preceding `23ff8f588` head passed complete-schema, PostgreSQL task/API/RACI suites and generated API contracts. Local Docker was unresponsive; no local Docker rehearsal pass is claimed for this integration. The native PostgreSQL HTTP result is separate evidence.\n- Earlier event implementation validation includes eight isolated runtime suites, eight real RACI desktop/phone browser cases and formal negative controls, retained in the audit record. These are historical results, not substitutes for the new head's CI.\n\nMerge gates: all prescribed checks must pass on the current head; obtain fresh independent approval and recheck head/base/threads/compatibility. The mobile companion is already integrated. No source PR is superseded until this replacement actually merges. No deployment, feature activation, branch deletion, force push or administrator bypass is authorized by this implementation.\n\n\n### Task-completion expiry polling correction\n\nCurrent head `154f968aa99780723e1d365c827010d8d85220a3` preserves the lifecycle fixes in34ca75d. The hosted PostgreSQL task-completion job failed with exit1 and no assertion diagnostic. Inspection found a15-second expiry window bounded by100 polls sleeping0.1seconds: on a fast runner that can time out before expiry. This follow-up allows200 polls and adds a precise timeout diagnostic, retaining every before-expiry, exact-blocker, after-expiry, denial, revision, history and rollback assertion.\n\nThe complete unchanged-source baseline passed locally because query overhead extends the window; this is not claimed as a reproduced CI failure. The corrected complete native PostgreSQL16 suite also passed:32 decision cases,12 RC/RR/Serializable races, four observed expiry waits, revocation ordering, rollback/reapply and aborted-first recovery. Shell syntax, whitespace, three specification-inventory tests and the generated inventory check pass. Fresh current-head hosted checks and independent approval remain required.\n",
